  "term": "meningococcal meningitis",
  "definition": "Meningococcal meningitis is a severe, sudden infection caused by Neisseria meningitidis that can produce fever, rash, irritation of the meninges, meningitis, and sometimes death. It is a major public health problem worldwide and can leave some survivors with long-term neurological complications.",
